# Citation metadata. GitHub renders this into a "Cite this repository"
# button.
#
# `doi` is the VERSION DOI, reserved on Zenodo BEFORE the tag - the same
# reserve-first route as DL-TerrainDiversity and DL-TerrainSlicer. That order
# is what lets the archived snapshot carry a citation file that knows its own
# identifier; the Zenodo-GitHub integration would mint it only after the tag,
# so the deposit would name a DOI it does not have. Every release reserves a
# NEW one (Zenodo record -> New version -> Get a DOI now!); never carry this
# one forward.
#
# `version` must equal the release tag without its "v".
#
# No e-mail address here, deliberately: a deposit is permanent in DataCite,
# and DL-TerrainSlicer's citation file carries none either.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DL-TerrainMapper"
message: "If you use this tool in a publication or in teaching, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ihle
    given-names: Marc-Eduard
    # Standing rule: a Digital Landscapes tool names Digital Landscapes,
    # never a university.
    affiliation: "Digital Landscapes"
abstract: >-
  A laser-cut map compiler. Terrain and field observations go in; a fabricable
  drawing comes out - engraved contours, labelled heights, hachures, located
  photograph marks, halftones, sections and thresholded material regions -
  where the symbology maps to laser operations instead of to screen pixels.
  One raster can be translated seven ways at once, and the translations
  compose rather than exclude. Shapefile and GML features carry
  attribute-driven styling, and a clip-to-tile stage runs last, so every
  pattern is anchored to the ground rather than to a plate and two
  neighbouring plates cannot disagree. Four ways out - DXF, SVG, a greyscale
  raster engrave with its cut lines beside it, and shapefiles back to QGIS -
  all render the same compiled drawing, so the preview cannot disagree with
  the file. Runs entirely in the browser with no build step, no dependencies
  and no network calls: field photographs are read in the tab and never leave
  the machine.
keywords:
  - laser cutting
  - cartography
  - map
  - terrain model
  - digital terrain model
  - field observation
  - digital fabrication
  - DXF
  - SVG
  - GeoTIFF
  - shapefile
  - GML
  - landscape architecture
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/DLandscapes/dl-terrain-mapper"
url: "https://digital-landscapes.com/terrain-mapper/"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23512188"
